36.1 Conservative invalidation

When Stage N changes, the application invalidates later:
- accepted changes;
- current canonical records;
- prompts;
- pending proposals;
- confirmations;
- convergence;
- release;
- artifact-identity batches;
- evidence-chain batches;
- delivery authorization.

Complex field-level dependency invalidation does not replace conservative stage invalidation unless conservative invalidation becomes demonstrably unusable.

